{
  "_comment": [
    "OpenVPN client — driven via systemd's openvpn-client@.service.",
    "",
    "Place your .ovpn at /etc/openvpn/client/<name>.conf (root-",
    "owned). If the .ovpn doesn't embed credentials, also drop",
    "/etc/openvpn/client/<name>.creds (two lines: user, password)",
    "and add `auth-user-pass <name>.creds` to the .conf. Then set",
    "the profile name in the field below.",
    "",
    "Connect / disconnect run `systemctl start|stop",
    "openvpn-client@<name>` and polkit decides — Nirimaki installs a",
    "polkit rule (during this template's Install step) that grants",
    "wheel-group users on a local active session passwordless",
    "control of openvpn-client@*.service. So after Install,",
    "connect/disconnect just work, no prompt.",
    "",
    "For an importable / GUI workflow, NetworkManager's OpenVPN",
    "plugin (`nm-connection-editor`) is friendlier — those profiles",
    "auto-appear in this same popover via nmcli."
  ],
  "id":   "openvpn",
  "name": "OpenVPN",
  "icon": "󰒃",
  "multiInstance": true,

  "install": {
    "package": "openvpn",
    "binary":  "openvpn",
    "hint":    "Provides the openvpn binary + openvpn-client@.service unit. Place your .ovpn at /etc/openvpn/client/<name>.conf (root-owned) before connecting.",
    "postInstall": [
      ["sudo", "install", "-m", "0644",
       "$NIRIMAKI_REPO/default/polkit/50-nirimaki-openvpn.rules",
       "/etc/polkit-1/rules.d/50-nirimaki-openvpn.rules"]
    ]
  },

  "fields": [
    { "key":   "profileName",
      "label": "Profile name",
      "help":  "Base name of /etc/openvpn/client/<name>.conf.",
      "type":  "text",
      "value": "client" }
  ],

  "statusCmd":        ["systemctl", "is-active", "openvpn-client@{{profileName}}"],
  "statusOnPattern":  "^active$",
  "statusLabelCmd":   ["sh", "-lc", "ip -o -4 addr show tun0 2>/dev/null | awk '{print $4}' | cut -d/ -f1"],
  "connectCmd":       ["systemctl", "start", "openvpn-client@{{profileName}}"],
  "disconnectCmd":    ["systemctl", "stop",  "openvpn-client@{{profileName}}"],
  "pollSeconds":      5
}
